From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:48:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 420/420] arm64: dts: qcom: ipq9574: describe IMEM and the
 restart reason

Add the IMEM (on-chip SRAM) node and point the watchdog at the restart
reason word in it, so that qcom-wdt can report a watchdog reset in
/sys/class/watchdog/watchdog0/bootstatus. The EXPIRED_STATUS bit in
WDT_STS that the driver checks otherwise is already cleared when Linux
boots.

The IMEM node is Kathiravan Thirumoorthy's "arm64: dts: qcom: ipq9574:
Add the IMEM node" (v3 5/6), unchanged. That series got "changes
requested" for its binding (the reviewers want the IMEM binding posted
complete, with its children), not for the node itself. The child node
and the watchdog "sram" property follow his IPQ5424 patch, which is in
linux-next ("arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5424: add support to get watchdog
bootstatus from IMEM", v11 3/3).

The offset is IPQ9574 specific: the QSDK 12.x ipq9574.dtsi describes
the restart reason as "restart-reason-buf-addr@7a4" in the IMEM at
0x08600000, and its qti_scm_restart_reason driver decodes 0x1 as a
non-secure watchdog reset and 0x20 as a power-on reset. Those are the
values that mainline commit 6a393b0ea3cc ("watchdog: qcom: report
bootstatus on IPQ9574 and IPQ5332") uses for IPQ9574 (CARDRESET and
POWERUNDER).

Without the sram property the driver falls back to the old WDT_STS
check, so dropping this patch restores the previous behaviour.

Based on patches by Kathiravan Thirumoorthy
<kathiravan.thirumoorthy@oss.qualcomm.com>.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260228-imem-v3-5-20fbcc1a9404@oss.qualcomm.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260727-wdt_reset_reason-v11-3-eeedb22beefe@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: Crescentm <guyues@outlook.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
index ad49949c0..20601b675 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq9574.dtsi
@@ -772,6 +772,21 @@ usb_0_qmpphy: usb-phy@7d000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		sram@8600000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,ipq9574-imem", "mmio-sram";
+			reg = <0x08600000 0x8000>;
+			ranges = <0 0x08600000 0x8000>;
+
+			no-memory-wc;
+
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+
+			restart_reason: restartreason-sram@7a4 {
+				reg = <0x7a4 0x4>;
+			};
+		};
+
 		usb3: usb@8af8800 {
 			compatible = "qcom,ipq9574-dwc3", "qcom,dwc3";
 			reg = <0x08af8800 0x400>;
@@ -855,6 +870,7 @@ watchdog: watchdog@b017000 {
 			reg = <0x0b017000 0x1000>;
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 3 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 			clocks = <&sleep_clk>;
+			sram = <&restart_reason>;
 			timeout-sec = <30>;
 		};
 
